# Everything the image must not carry. A build context that includes .env or
# .git is how a secret ends up in a published layer.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backups
storage
docs
*.md
!README.md
# apps/agent and apps/portal are NOT excluded here, though the API images
# never copy them.
#
# Excluding them was correct for the API image and fatal for the other two,
# whose entire source lives there. `Dockerfile.agent.dockerignore` and
# `Dockerfile.portal.dockerignore` were added to override this file for those
# builds — but `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` is a BuildKit convention, and a
# builder that does not implement it falls back to this file and fails on
# `COPY apps/agent ./apps/agent` with "not found". GitHub Actions honours the
# convention; Railway's Metal builder is a different implementation and
# correctness should not rest on whether it agrees.
#
# Leaving them in costs the API build a larger context and nothing in the
# shipped image: no Dockerfile here does a bare `COPY .`, so every image takes
# only the paths it names. Checked before removing these two lines.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
